<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n109657" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπωμοσία</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>oath taken in court to delay
				proceedings</i> (v. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπόμνυμι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			), </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>oath</i> or <i>affidavit showing good ground for the
			absence</i> of a party to a suit, <i>application for delay,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
				21.84
			</span></i> (pl.), v.
			<i><span class="en">
				Harp.
			</span></i> s. v.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπωμοσίαν παραδέχεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hyp.
					<u>Eux.</u>
					7
				</span></i>
			; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνθυπόμνυμι.</span>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>oath</i> taken by the prosecutor in a <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γραφὴ παρανόμων</span> (v. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παράνομος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.2
				</span></i>
			), with the effect of suspending the proposed law or decree,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐᾶν [τὸν νόμον] ἐν ὑ.</span> to
			leave it in <i>the condition caused by the</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπωμοσία,</span> to let it drop, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				18.103
			</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>AB</u>
				313
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				8.56
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
